    {
      "title": "Further bomb threats disrupt at least another 18 flights across Europe",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/06/further-bomb-threats-disrupt-flights-across-europe",
      "description": "<p>Media organisations in Ireland and UK also affected as apparently coordinated effort to cause chaos continues</p><p>A fresh wave of bomb threats disrupted air traffic across<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/europe-news\"> Europe </a>on Friday but the affected aircraft landed safely and searches revealed no explosive devices.</p><p>The latest alerts affected at least 18 flights to or from Bulgaria, Cyprus, Czechia, France, Hungary, Italy, Portugal, Romania and the UK.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/06/further-bomb-threats-disrupt-flights-across-europe\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-06T17:14:31"
    },
    {
      "title": "Bomb threats against European flights ‘likely a coordinated campaign of disruption’, Ireland says – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/nov/06/high-alert-hoax-bomb-threats-france-air-lingus-belgium-pope-leo-europe-live",
      "description": "<p>This blog is now closed, you can read more on this story <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/06/further-bomb-threats-disrupt-flights-across-europe\">here</a></p><p><strong>A Romanian airline Tarom flight from Prague to Bucharest is the latest believed to be affected by today’s bomb threats.</strong></p><p>The aircraft, operating flight number ROT226M, sent a squawk code of 7700 – general emergency – before landing safely in Bucharest. The threat was later confirmed to be unproven.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/nov/06/high-alert-hoax-bomb-threats-france-air-lingus-belgium-pope-leo-europe-live\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-06T16:26:17"
    },
    {
      "title": "Most Europeans want action to tackle climate crisis but not at any cost, poll shows",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/06/europeans-want-action-climate-crisis-yougov-poll",
      "description": "<p>YouGov survey finds support for tree planting and emissions taxes but opposition to air travel and fuel levies</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/nov/06/high-alert-hoax-bomb-threats-france-air-lingus-belgium-pope-leo-europe-live\">Europe live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Europeans believe human-made climate change is real, a survey has shown, with most feeling action must be taken soon – as long as they do not have to sacrifice too much to achieve it.</p><p>The YouGov poll of six European countries showed between 69% (Germany) and 80% (France) of respondents believed the climate was changing, with few (1%-4%) denying it and 14-20% believing it was changing, but not as a result of human activity.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/06/europeans-want-action-climate-crisis-yougov-poll\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-06T12:27:54"
    },
    {
      "title": "Bomb Threats in Europe Probably a Coordinated Campaign, Ireland Says",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/06/world/europe/bomb-threats-flights-campaign-ireland.html",
      "description": "Multiple flights in Europe were disrupted and several newsrooms in Ireland were evacuated after false bomb threats, the latest of a series of security incidents.",
      "source_name": "NYT World News",
      "published": "2026-11-06T20:07:48"
    },
    {
      "title": "Wave of Hoax Bomb Threats to Flights in Europe Leaves Travelers Frustrated",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/06/world/europe/bomb-threats-planes-flights-europe-travel.html",
      "description": "Bomb threats have disrupted dozens of flights in Europe over the past week. At airports in Rome, Madrid and Warsaw, travelers were more frustrated than fearful.",
      "source_name": "NYT World News",
      "published": "2026-11-06T16:21:25"
    }
